---
description: Manifest V3 service worker rules; no MV2 background-page code
globs: "**/sw.js,**/sw.ts,**/service-worker.*,**/service_worker.*,**/background.*,**/*-worker.*,**/manifest.json"
alwaysApply: false
---

The background script is an MV3 service worker. Chrome stops it after about 30 seconds idle.

| Never | Always |
|---|---|
| `let count = 0` as state | `chrome.storage.session` / `chrome.storage.local` |
| `setTimeout(fn, 60 * 60 * 1000)` | `chrome.alarms.create("name", { periodInMinutes: 60 })` |
| `addListener` inside a callback or after `await` | every `addListener` at the top level, synchronously |
| `document`, `window`, `localStorage`, `XMLHttpRequest` | `fetch`, `chrome.storage`, `chrome.offscreen` for DOM work |
| `chrome.browserAction`, `chrome.pageAction` | `chrome.action` |
| `chrome.tabs.executeScript` | `chrome.scripting.executeScript` |
| `chrome.extension.getBackgroundPage()` | `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` |
| `webRequest` with `["blocking"]` | `chrome.declarativeNetRequest` |
| `eval`, `new Function`, remote `<script src>` | code shipped in the package |

- An async `onMessage` reply needs `return true` from the listener.
- After editing, run the `mv3-worker-guard` skill's scanner, then restart the worker and use the feature again.
